 years or so, life on Earth was shaped by natural forces. Evolution tended to happen slowly, with species crafted across millennia. Then, a few hundred thousand years ago, along came a bolshie, big-brained, bipedal primate we now call Homo sapiens, and with that, the Earth's natural history came to an abrupt end. We are now living through the post-natural phase, where humans have become the leading force shaping evolution. This thought-provoking book considers the many ways that we've altered the DNA of living things and changed the fate of life on earth. We have carved chihuahuas from wolves and fancy chickens from jungle fowl.","thumbnailUrl":"/book-covers/book-life-changing-how-humans-are-altering-life-on-earth-helen-pilcher.jpg","readerProfile":{"readerLevel":"crossover","narrativeScore":0,"accessibilityScore":0,"scholarlyScore":0,"traits":[],"method":"deterministic_catalog_heuristics_v1"},"experimentalSemanticProfile":{"centralFigures":[],"centralPlaces":[],"argument":{"present":true,"statement":"Humans have become the leading force shaping evolution, altering living things’ DNA and thereby ending Earth’s prior natural history pattern.","confidence":0.74},"academicOrientation":{"score":38,"confidence":0.48},"profileConfidence":0.62,"model":"gpt-5.4-nano-2026-03-17","promptVersion":8,"inputHash":"7212c69d28025ab835ed969402c4b55d5d3fe9874f1fedf1b26aa8661ee66c0b","reviewStatus":"unreviewed","validationWarnings":[]},"displaySummary":"This thought-provoking book considers the many ways that we've altered the DNA of living things and changed the fate of life on earth. We have carved chihuahuas from wolves and fancy chickens from jungle fowl.","primarySubject":"Nature & Environment","primaryTopic":"Natural History & Animals","subjectEvidence":{"primarySubject":"Nature & Environment","confidence":"low","method":"evidence_score","candidates":[{"subject":"Nature & Environment","score":7,"evidenceCount":4},{"subject":"Science","score":3,"evidenceCount":2},{"subject":"Worl